how code runs:
source code -> compiler -> bytecode -> JVM(java virtual machine) -> machine code
java is a portable language because it can run on any platform that has a JVM installed. 
c++ is not a portable language because it is compiled directly to machine code, which is specific to the
operating system and hardware architecture. This means that a C++ program compiled on one platform may not 
run on another platform without recompilation.
